1. Environment I Am Building

I am developing the synthesis-route-gym environment to enable Agent Scientist to plan, evaluate, compare, and iteratively improve chemical synthesis routes for a given target molecule.

The environment is intended to accept a target molecule, available starting materials and reagents, and user-defined constraints. It will use existing Boltzmann platform capabilities and retrosynthesis research tools to generate candidate routes, assess their chemical feasibility, and rank them based on starting-material availability, reaction conditions, cost, and supporting evidence.

The planned specialist agents are:

Retrosynthesis Strategist: Generates and compares candidate synthetic routes.

Condition Optimisation Scientist: Evaluates and improves reaction conditions.

Route Critic: Reviews chemical feasibility, route constraints, and supporting evidence.

I will evaluate whether these specialists provide measurable improvements over direct tool execution and single-agent baselines before justifying additional agents.

